# Secrets - never commit
token.txt
# The literal name above was NOT enough. Her Discord token is not called
# token.txt - config.json points token_source at C:\Lulu\discord_token.txt, and
# the migration tools expected C:\lulu\lulu_token.txt. Neither matched the
# pattern, so either one would have landed as a committable secret, and
# pipeline.checkpoint() runs `git add -A` - the next self-edit would have put
# her live token in history with nobody deciding to. Match the shape, not one
# spelling of it.
*token*.txt
brain_key.txt
config.json
.env
# MCP credential values. Named here for a mechanical reason, not tidiness: the
# pipeline's checkpoint runs `git add -A - discord/`, so any new file in this
# folder is swept into a commit the next time a self-edit is processed. A
# secrets file that is not ignored gets committed by the machinery itself.
mcp_secrets.json

# Runtime
#
# memory/ used to be ignored wholesale, which was harmless while this tree had no
# repo. It is NOT harmless now: the den-memory store lives at memory/store.py, and
# an ignore of the whole folder would leave CODE untracked while ignoring the data
# beside it. Ignore the runtime data, keep the source.
memory/*
!memory/store.py
!memory/test_store.py
logs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Staging area for self-edits. Runtime state, and the pipeline's checkpoint
# commits with `git add -A - discord/`, so without this line a rejected or
# staged patch gets swept into git history. That happened once already.
pending/

# Where the smoke test redirects every live path so no check can write a file a
# running process acts on. Throwaway, one per run (pid-suffixed), recreated each
# time.
.smoke_sandbox*/

# The trial: a throwaway copy of her folder with the staged text poured over it,
# where the smoke test is run BEFORE anything is staged. Ignored for the same
# reason as the sandbox above, and ignored BEFORE it exists: it is deleted at the
# end of every trial, so the only way this line ever matters is a crash mid-trial
# - and pipeline.py's checkpoint runs `git add -A`, which would commit the whole
# copy of her folder rather than the one file she was changing.
.trial/

# Chatter cooldown state - channel id to timestamp, rewritten as she talks.
# Runtime data like memory/, not source.
chatter.json

# The purse and its price cache. Both are rewritten as she talks, and the
# pipeline's checkpoint runs `git add -A - discord/` - so unignored, every
# self-edit would commit today's spending total and a price dump into history.
# The ledger is deliberately NOT under memory/: that tier is sealed, which is
# why the first version of the cap could never write its total at all.
spend.json
price_cache.json

# whisper.cpp - the build, its DLLs and 1.8 GB of models. Master's build, not
# den source, and it must stay invisible to the machinery: pipeline.py's
# checkpoint runs `git add -A - discord/`, so unignored this whole tree would be
# swept into a commit the next time she self-edits. Resolved at runtime only.
whisper.cpp/

# A node runtime she can execute, plus the cache npx downloads into. Same rule as
# whisper.cpp and for the same reason: pipeline.py's checkpoint runs
# `git add -A - discord/`, so 107 MB of runtime would be committed by the next
# self-edit. Ignored BEFORE it exists, and pointed at from mcp.json rather than
# from any PATH - run-bot.cmd sets no PATH at all, and the machine's own node
# lives inside a human's profile while she runs as the lulu-bot account.
node/
node_cache/

# Which start I have already announced, so a crash loop cannot turn into one
# message per attempt. Runtime state like chatter.json, and the pipeline's
# checkpoint runs `git add -A - discord/`, so unignored this little file would be
# committed by the next self-edit.
restart_seen.json

# Which changelog entries I have already been shown. Same tier as restart_seen
# above and the same reason: runtime state, and the next self-edit's checkpoint
# would otherwise commit it. CHANGELOG.md itself is deliberately NOT ignored -
# that one is the record of what was done to me and belongs in git.
changelog_seen.json

# ffmpeg, dropped in by hand for voice-message transcription. Same rule as
# whisper.cpp and node/, for the same reason: the pipeline's checkpoint runs
# `git add -A - discord/`, and this is 242 MB - unignored it would be committed by
# the next self-edit rather than by anyone deciding to. Resolved at runtime only,
# by whisper_stt, which looks beside her before it looks at PATH.
ffmpeg/

# The open long-task. Rewritten every turn while a task runs, and the pipeline's
# checkpoint runs `git add -A - discord/` - so unignored, every self-edit would
# commit whatever the current job happened to be mid-flight. Runtime state like
# chatter.json and spend.json, not source. It cannot live under memory/: that
# tier is sealed, and the first version of the purse made exactly that mistake.
task.json

# The interpreter she runs on, now that it lives beside her instead of in the
# den. 110 MB of runtime, and pipeline.py's checkpoint runs `git add -A`, so
# unignored it would be committed by the next self-edit rather than by anyone
# deciding to. Same rule as node/ and whisper.cpp/.
Python311/

# Migration scratch: rename.py and relabel_memory.py did their one job and are
# parked, not shipped. Throwaway tooling, like the den's scratch\ folder.
.setup-tools/

# Nana's old scratch, carried over by the clone and pointed at the pre-flatten
# path. Deletable; not source.
tmp_*.py

# Anything she installs for herself. Broad on purpose, and here is why it has to
# be: she can now run commands in her own folder, so a venv, a root-level
# node_modules, or a downloaded browser build can appear here at any time - and
# pipeline.py's checkpoint runs `git add -A`, so unignored they would be
# committed by the NEXT SELF-EDIT rather than by anyone deciding to. Same rule as
# node/, ffmpeg/ and Python311/, and ignored BEFORE they exist for the same
# reason those were: the one time this was missed, 242 MB of ffmpeg sat one
# self-edit away from the history.
ms-playwright/
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
# Where the playwright MCP server drops its console logs and page snapshots. It is
# NOT ms-playwright/ - that is the browser build, this is the scratch the tools
# write on every single browser call, into the working directory. Ignored for the
# same reason as everything else above: checkpoint runs `git add -A`, so one
# browser call followed by one self-edit would put page dumps in her history.
# Found 2026-09-20 by running `git add -A --dry-run` after a browser test, having
# first believed it was covered because the names look alike.
.playwright-mcp/

# The persistent browser profile, added to mcp.json as `--user-data-dir` on
# 2026-09-20 so a login can survive a restart. Without that flag the MCP server
# uses a TEMPORARY directory, so master's plan of "headed once, log in, done"
# would have looked like it worked and then silently evaporated.
#
# THIS ONE HOLDS LIVE SESSION COOKIES for whatever he logs into - which makes it
# the first entry here that is a credential rather than runtime scratch. The
# reason it needs a line at all is the same mechanical one as everything above:
# pipeline.checkpoint() runs `git add -A`, so unignored the next self-edit would
# commit his social media sessions into her history with nobody deciding to.
# Ignored BEFORE the folder held anything, because the first time this pattern
# was missed - ffmpeg, 242 MB - it was found one self-edit away from the history.
#
# Flagged to master on top of the ignore: the profile sits inside C:/lulu and her
# read_file has NO read guard, so she can read her own session cookies. That is
# not a leak to a stranger and it is not fixed by this line - it is a fact about
# where the thing lives, and it is written down so nobody discovers it by
# accident later.
browser-profile/
brain_keys.json
browser/instagram_jar.json
# The reddit / X / instagram / google session cookies, injected at startup the
# same way the instagram jar is. Named here BEFORE the file existed, on purpose:
# a jar of live session values that is not ignored gets swept into her history by
# the next self-edit's `git add -A`, which is how ffmpeg nearly landed and how
# mcp_secrets.json would have. Written 2026-09-21, when the profile's own cookie
# store came up empty and master signed back in on his own Canary so this could
# be rebuilt.
#
# Also NOT fixed by this line, and worth knowing: the jar sits inside C:/lulu and
# her read_file has no read guard, so she can read her own session cookies. Same
# fact as the browser-profile note above - not a leak to a stranger, just true.
browser/social_jar.json
